Privacy Policy
Last updated: 15 August 2026
This Privacy Policy explains how MAmac ("we", "us") collects, uses, and protects your information when you use our platform to find and manage professional connections.
1. Information we collect
	•	Account details you provide, such as your name, email address, and password.
	•	Membership information, including your name, contact details, and booking history.
	•	Usage data, such as connections made, messages sent, and time spent on the platform.
	•	Device and log data, such as IP address, browser type, and access times.
2. How we use your information
	•	To create and manage your membership account.
	•	To process your bookings and manage capacity across facilities.
	•	To send you service updates, booking confirmations, and reminders.
	•	To maintain the security and integrity of the platform.
3. How we share information
We share limited booking details (such as your name and reservation time) with on-site staff so they can confirm your visit. We do not sell your personal information. We may share data with service providers who help us operate MAmac, under confidentiality obligations, or when required by law.
4. Data retention
We retain your account and activity data for as long as your membership is active, and for a reasonable period afterward to comply with legal obligations or resolve disputes.
5. Your rights
	•	Access, correct, or delete your personal information at any time from your account settings.
	•	Opt out of non-essential communications.
	•	Request a copy of the data we hold about you.
6. Security
We use industry-standard safeguards to protect your information, including encryption in transit and access controls. No system is completely secure, so we encourage you to use a strong, unique password.
7. Contact us
If you have questions about this policy or how your data is handled, contact us at privacy@mamac.example.
This is placeholder policy text for demonstration purposes and should be reviewed by legal counsel before use with real members.
